{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1091858-missing-realms","id":1091858,"title":"Missing Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T01:00:24-07:00","id":1091858,"title":"Missing Realms","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">There are two pieces of text related to Realms and spending Glamour on page 232:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">In order to use a cantrip on a desired subject, the changeling normally must have purchased the relevant Realm (or Realms) up to the dot rating that best describes her target. However, if she lacks an appropriate rating, then all is not lost the changeling may fold together imagination, Glamour, aspiration, and will to force the magic to bend to her will anyway.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Players may target a cantrip with Realm ratings they haven\u2019t purchased by spending a point of Glamour per &quot;missing&quot; Realm.</b></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Note: they actually follow each other but I've quoted separately for clarity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The first implies that if you do not have the dot rating for the relevant Realm, something extra is required.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The second states that you only need to spend a point of Glamour per missing Realm (even though it first mentions Realm ratings that haven't been purchsed).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So if a character has only </span></span><b>Fae 2</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> but wishes to perform a Cantrip requiring </span></span><b>Fae 5</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> (say, targeting a Cantrip), does the character need to spend an additional point of Glamour or not? The second text mentions missing Realm ratings, but only requires a point of Glamour per missing Realm. Should the second text actually say something like:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Players may target a cantrip with Realm ratings they haven\u2019t purchased by spending a point of Glamour per &quot;missing&quot; Realm </b></span></span></span><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">rating</span></b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>.</b></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","user":"Shining Dragon","date":". 05-13-2017, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:11:24-07:00","id":1091862,"title":"","content":"I've posted this question in the Errata thread as well, since I suspect it needs clarification in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T07:38:25-07:00","id":1091941,"title":"","content":"As per Matt in another thread, if you need fae 5 but don't have fae 5 you spend only one point of Glamour, be it your rating in Fae is 4 or 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}